\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Dear Lord and Father of mankind,
\par Forgive our foolish ways;
\par Reclothe us in our rightful mind:
\par In purer lives Thy service find,
\par In deeper reverence, praise.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. In simple trust like theirs who heard,
\par Beside the Syrian sea,
\par The gracious calling of th Lord,
\par Let us, like them, without a word
\par Rise up and follow Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. O Sabbath rest by Galilee!
\par O calm of hills above,
\par Where Jesus knelt to share with Thee
\par The silence of eternity,
\par Interpreted by love!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. With that deep hush subduing all
\par Our words and works that drown
\par The tender whisper of Thy call,
\par As noiseless let Thy blessing fall
\par As fell Thy manna down.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Drop Thy still dews of quietness,
\par Till all our strivings cease;
\par Take from our souls the strain
\par and stress,
\par And let our ordered lives confess
\par The beauty of Thy peace.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Breathe through the heats of our 
\par desire
\par Thy coolness and Thy balm;
\par Let sense be dumb, let flesh retire;
\par Speak through the earthquake,
\par wind, and fire,
\par O still small voice of calm!
\par                           Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

